.TH SSMCPD 8 "2026-11-16" "ssmcp 0.4.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
ssmcpd \- SSH-authenticated MCP gateway for local shells and coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ssmcpd serve
.RB [ \-\-config " path" ]
.RB [ \-\-public-url " https://host" ]
.RB [ \-\-listen " 127.0.0.1:8080" ]
.RB [ \-\-socket " path" ]
.RB [ \-\-access-token-ttl " seconds" ]
.RB [ \-\-refresh-token-idle-ttl " seconds" ]
.RB [ \-\-refresh-token-max-ttl " seconds" ]
.RB [ \-\-client-registration-ttl " seconds" ]
.PP
.B ssmcpd attach
.RB [ \-\-socket " path" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The serve command listens for MCP HTTP requests and authenticated local bridge
connections. A reverse proxy supplies public HTTPS. Clients with an allow list
use /mcp and GitHub identity authorization. Clients without an allow list retain
the SSH account's /username endpoint and one-time login code. Each connection
has an independent random client ID. Up to 128 clients may attach to one SSH account.
.PP
The attach command is run by OpenSSH as a ForceCommand. It forwards standard input
and output to the daemon's Unix socket. The daemon obtains the account identity
from kernel peer credentials. Client names, hostnames, working directories and
backend types are discovery metadata, not authentication fields.
.PP
The external MCP tool catalog contains exactly list and code_mode. The native
capability names for shell, codex, cc, pi and opencode remain accessible inside
code_mode; they are not individually advertised as external MCP tools.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Read a TOML configuration file for serve. SSMCP_CONFIG selects an explicit file
when this option is absent. Otherwise /etc/ssmcpd/ssmcpd.toml is loaded if it exists.
An explicitly selected missing or invalid file is an error.
.TP
.BI \-\-public-url " url"
Public HTTPS origin used to construct MCP URLs and validate Origin headers.
May also be configured by server.public_url in TOML or SSMCP_PUBLIC_URL.
.TP
.BI \-\-listen " address"
Loopback HTTP socket address. The default is 127.0.0.1:8080.
.TP
.BI \-\-socket " path"
Unix control socket path. The default is /run/ssmcpd/control.sock.
.TP
.BI \-\-access-token-ttl " seconds"
Access-token lifetime. The default is 28800 seconds (8 hours).
The environment variable is SSMCP_ACCESS_TOKEN_TTL.
.TP
.BI \-\-refresh-token-idle-ttl " seconds"
Refresh-token idle lifetime. Each successful refresh starts a new idle period,
bounded by the original authorization-family deadline. The default is 2592000
seconds (30 days). The environment variable is SSMCP_REFRESH_TOKEN_IDLE_TTL.
.TP
.BI \-\-refresh-token-max-ttl " seconds"
Maximum authorization-family lifetime measured from its initial authorization.
Refreshes do not extend this deadline. The default is 7776000 seconds (90 days).
The environment variable is SSMCP_REFRESH_TOKEN_MAX_TTL.
.TP
.BI \-\-client-registration-ttl " seconds"
OAuth client-registration and client-secret lifetime. The default is 31536000
seconds (365 days). The environment variable is SSMCP_CLIENT_REGISTRATION_TTL.
.PP
Lifetime options apply to serve. They accept positive integer seconds and require
access <= idle <= max <= registration <= 315360000 (3650 days).
Configuration precedence is command line, environment, TOML, then defaults.
The packaged systemd unit may read variables from /etc/ssmcpd/ssmcpd.env.
Changes take effect when the daemon starts; restarting clears OAuth state.
.SH TOML AND GITHUB
The server section accepts listen, public_url and socket. The oauth section
accepts access_token_ttl, refresh_token_idle_ttl, refresh_token_max_ttl and
client_registration_ttl as integer seconds. The auth.github section contains
client_id and client_secret from a GitHub OAuth App. Omit that section when
only login-code authorization is required.
.PP
Configure the GitHub OAuth App callback as the public HTTPS origin followed by
/oauth/callback/github. The server derives this callback from public_url. A
secret-bearing TOML file must be private; use mode 0600 and make it owned by the
ssmcpd service user. Keep client secrets out of source repositories and command
arguments. Existing environment or command-line values can override TOML values.
.PP
GitHub login requests no repository or email scopes. The upstream access token
is used to fetch the authenticated user identity and is not retained. ssmcp
issues its own access and refresh tokens for MCP operations.
.SH DISCOVERY AND EXECUTION
The list tool returns online clients permitted by the current authorization,
including IDs, names, backend types, hostnames and startup directories. A client_id
argument selects a paginated native capability catalog. Duplicate display names
are allowed; dispatch always uses the connection ID.
.PP
The code_mode tool starts a system-installed Node.js process inside bubblewrap
for each invocation. Its host calls select a client by ID and forward native
operations over the existing SSH bridge. The public JavaScript API provides
clients, call, tools and logging. The worker does not inherit server credentials
or mount the host's working directories, home directories or control socket.
.PP
Install Node.js 18 or newer, bubblewrap 0.8 or newer and util-linux prlimit using
the operating system package manager. The process-count limit is applied inside
the new user namespace, so existing host-user threads do not block its creation. No npm package is required. The bridge script is installed at
PREFIX/libexec/ssmcp/code-mode.js, normally
/usr/local/libexec/ssmcp/code-mode.js. SSMCP_CODE_MODE_RUNNER may select an
absolute script path in the server environment.
.PP
Node.js vm contexts and permission flags are not security boundaries for
untrusted code. Linux isolation is provided by bubblewrap; missing dependencies
or unavailable namespaces produce an error, without falling back to direct
Node.js execution. The list tool remains available.
.PP
Code source, runtime memory, execution time, host calls, logs and results are
bounded. Each native call checks the current authorization and target access again.
A timeout stops the script, but does not roll back actions already submitted to
a native backend. Calls with an uncertain outcome should not be blindly retried.
.PP
The V8 old-generation heap is limited to 32 MiB. Linux RLIMIT_DATA is 256 MiB
and RLIMIT_AS is 2 GiB; these are data and virtual-address-space limits, not a
claim that total process memory is 32 MiB. The worker CPU limit is 2 seconds.
.SH AUTHORIZATION LIFETIME
The gateway serves OAuth discovery, dynamic client registration, authorization
and token endpoints. On /mcp, GitHub login verifies the user; a separate ssmcp
consent screen displays that identity, the MCP client name, registered callback
origin, resource and current permitted-session count. The user must explicitly
allow that MCP client. Consent can succeed with no matching sessions online;
discovery then returns an empty list until an allowed connection appears.
.PP
The server resolves each allow-listed username to a stable GitHub user ID at
attachment. Discovery and calls compare the verified ID with each connection's
allow list. Rename pinning lasts for that connection only; a new attachment
resolves the supplied usernames again. No persistent identity pins are stored.
.PP
On /username, the one-time login-code method remains available. Both methods
complete Authorization Code with S256 PKCE. HTTP MCP requests carry a ssmcp
access token as their Bearer credential.
.PP
GitHub grants authorize current and future connections that explicitly allow
the verified identity and are not anchored to an issuing SSH connection.
Login-code grants authorize only connections without an allow list under the
same Linux account while the source SSH connection remains live. They cannot
enumerate or call an allow-listed connection. Client IDs alone do not confer access.
.PP
Login codes and authorization-form transactions expire after 30 minutes.
Login codes are consumed by successful authorization. The OAuth authorization
code returned to the client expires after 60 seconds and requires its PKCE verifier.
Access tokens default to at most 8 hours. Refresh tokens rotate on successful use;
their default 30-day idle period slides forward on each refresh, within a fixed
90-day authorization-family lifetime measured from initial authorization.
Client registrations and secrets default to 365 days. Token lifetimes are also
bounded by the remaining authorization and registration lifetimes.
.PP
Omitting grant_types during registration provisions authorization_code and
refresh_token and returns both in the registration response. Explicitly
registering only authorization_code continues to omit refresh tokens.
.PP
The MCP client implements silent renewal: before access-token expiry, or after
a 401 Bearer challenge with error="invalid_token", it sends grant_type=refresh_token,
its latest refresh token, the original resource URL and its registered client
authentication to the token endpoint. It must save both newly returned tokens
and replace its old refresh token before another refresh. Serialize refreshes
for one grant; replaying an already consumed refresh token revokes that grant.
Access-token expiry alone does not require interactive login.
.PP
Disconnecting a local client removes that session and backend. A GitHub grant
can remain valid and access other matching sessions or a newly attached allowed
session. A login-code grant is revoked when its issuing connection disconnects.
Registrations and OAuth state are in memory and end when the daemon exits, so
a daemon restart requires registration and login again in both modes.
.SH DEPLOYMENT
Run the daemon as an unprivileged service account. Restrict access to the control
socket with a dedicated group. Configure OpenSSH AuthenticationMethods publickey,
ForceCommand ssmcpd attach, DisableForwarding yes and PermitTTY no for this group.
.PP
Install and configure the selected backend on each client. The daemon does not
need Codex, Claude Code, Pi or OpenCode installed. Backend operations use the
client user's permissions; native requests and approvals remain explicit.
.PP
Unprivileged user and network namespaces must be available to bubblewrap. Keep
NoNewPrivileges enabled and allow AF_NETLINK in RestrictAddressFamilies so
bubblewrap can configure loopback inside the isolated network namespace.
The unit keeps ProtectKernelTunables enabled with an exception for /proc/sys/user
so bubblewrap can set limits in its own user namespace. Host kernel permissions
still apply. Do not use RestrictNamespaces=yes for this service. Follow
distribution AppArmor or SELinux policy when namespace setup is restricted.
.PP
Version 0.4.0 keeps private bridge protocol version 4. Existing clients without
an allow list retain login-code behavior. To use GitHub authorization, upgrade
both programs and configure the provider. Unsupported older servers reject
allow-list metadata; new clients also reject a legacy login-code response when
an allow policy was requested. Updating source does not replace installed binaries.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ssmcpd/ssmcpd.toml
Default optional TOML configuration. Protect provider secrets with mode 0600.
.TP
.I /etc/ssmcpd/ssmcpd.env
Environment configuration for the packaged systemd unit.
.TP
.I /run/ssmcpd/control.sock
Default control socket. Its mode is 0660.
.TP
.I /usr/local/libexec/ssmcp/code-mode.js
Default installed JavaScript bridge script; changes with the installation prefix.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssmcp (1),
.BR sshd (8),
.BR sshd_config (5),
.BR systemd.service (5)

.SH PERSISTENT CLIENT REGISTRATION
The installed systemd service uses StateDirectory=ssmcpd (mode 0700).
OAuth client registrations are stored in oauth-clients.toml (mode 0600).
Set oauth.client_registry in TOML, SSMCP_CLIENT_REGISTRY, or
.B --client-registry PATH
to select another private file. Save failures reject registration with HTTP 503.
Corrupt files, unsafe permissions, issuer mismatch and lock conflicts fail startup.
Access tokens, refresh tokens and pending authorization remain process-local.
